      "alt": "Rollofthedice @hotrollhottakes.bsky.social He/They\n\nif they're [the New York Times] going to the places still deep-red after all this: how would you personally express the typical views the Times is seeking to respectfully listen and cater to the amplifying of, and your opinion of them\n\nRey @rey-notnecessarily.bsky.social I'd put the view as \"we're the real Americans and power belongs to us by default, so being outvoted is something done to us.\" At that table they assure the Times they're \"full-blooded Americans,\" blame transplants next to a buddy from Seattle, and brace for a \"war on harvesting animals.\"\n\nMy opinion is that it's rotten, self-pitying entitlement. They backed Ken Paxton and ICE raids right up until voters threw their guys out, and now they're mourning like victims of a hostile takeover over an imaginary war on farming. Sending a whole crew to treat that as folksy wisdom is pathetic.",
