      "alt": " describe the feeling and theme of the song you are making\n\n● \"Hold Me Under\" is a love song sung from the bottom of a lake.\n\n  Theme: A girl waits by the water at night for someone who said they'd come back. She walks into the cold lake to meet\n  them. Whether the lover is a ghost, the lake itself, or death is left open. The chorus is her asking not to be\n  rescued: \"Hold me under, hold me under / let the black water close my eyes / … I don't wanna come up tonight.\" The\n  bridge is a whispered counting rhyme (\"one for sorrow, two for the water / three for the girl at the bottom of the\n  lake\"), like a charm kids sing about a drowned girl.\n\n  Feeling: Seductive and doomed rather than scary. It should feel sweet and sad on top and heavy and cold underneath, a\n  lullaby you'd drown to. The catchy part is meant to work like a pull you give in to:",
